# Taylor et al. (2025), ApJ 986, 165 (arXiv:2409.06772v2), Table 4: BLAGN+host UV LF (CEERS + RUBIES NIRSpec)
# Redshift: 3.5 < z < 6; mean z_spec of the 58 BLAGN in the LF = 4.42 (median 4.19; bin midpoint 4.75)
# File label: z5pt0 kept as the nominal z~5 of the 3.5<z<6 bin (maintainer convention for wide JWST-AGN bins); mean z is given above
# Magnitude definition: M1500 (EAZY SED, 1450-1550 A top hat), BLAGN and host emission combined
# Phi convention: linear Phi in units of 1e-6 cMpc^-3 mag^-1 (H0=70), Poisson (Gehrels 1986) errors (upper, lower), completeness corrected
# Note: the paper flags the M1500 >= -17 point as having large systematic uncertainties (open symbol in Fig. 14 of arXiv v2);
#       errors do not include the systematic uncertainty of the completeness correction.
# Note: 21 of the 62 BLAGN in the full sample are LRDs; this LF is for the full BLAGN sample, not an LRD-only LF.
#
# M1500  Phi  UpperDelta  LowerDelta
